{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 21, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Hark ye traveler bold whose heart doth yearn for lands afar\nLet quill and ink with haste compose thy journey o’er fair Japan\n\nPray mark these days with heed and honor well thy plan\n\n---\n**Day the First: Upon the Shores of Nippon Arrive**\nUpon Tokyo’s bustle thou shalt set thy foot\nWhere neon lights do dance and future’s whispers shout\nTo Shinjuku’s heart of beat thou dost repair\nAwe at Golden Gai’s lanes so quaint and rare\n\nWith sushi fresh and sharp as samurai’s blade\nIn Tsukiji’s market let thy taste be made\nThen on to Asakusa where temples stand so tall\nSenso-ji’s gates shall greet thee with a call\n\nAs twilight paints the sky with hues divine\nTo Akihabara’s glow thou mayst repair to fine\nWhere robots stir and maidens anime sing\nAnd geeks do gather where the future clings\n\n---\n**Day the Second: Through Time and Tea thou Shalt Pass**\nTo Nikko’s woods where shrines in mist do hide\nWhere Toshogu’s splendor doth with nature abide\nWith torii gates that rise from lake so deep\nKegon Falls shall send thy breath askew\n\nThen back to Tokyo where Kyoto’s trains do glide\nTo Nara’s plains where deer with men confide\nFeed the creatures with crackers sweet and fair\nThen bow to Buddha’s gaze so vast and rare\n\nAt evening’s fall to Gion’s streets thou go\nWhere geishas glide with grace both soft and slow\nIn tea houses old where whispers softly play\nSavor matcha’s bite and silence’s sway\n\n---\n**Day the Third: Kyoto’s Rhymes and Osaka’s Glee**\nWhere temples gleam like emeralds set in stone\nKinkaku-ji’s gold shall make thy heart unknown\nThrough Arashiyama’s bamboo grove thou tread\nWhere earth and sky in hush seem wed\n\nAt Fushimi’s terraces where sake doth flow\nWith vineyards clinging to the slopes below\nThen to Osaka’s heart where laughter rings so free\nDotonbori’s lights shall set thy soul aglow\n\nWith takoyaki balls that dance and pop so merry\nAnd okonomiyaki’s layers rich and cherry\nTo Osaka Castle’s stones thou’st turn thy gaze\nWhere history’s echoes through the streets amaze\n\n---\n**Day the Fourth: The Path of Samurai and Sacred Grounds**\nTo Hiroshima’s peace where souls in silence found\nA moment’s hush beneath the dome so round\nThen on to Miyajima where torii doth float\nOn waters calm where tides and time denote\n\nWith Koyasan’s monks in robes of indigo\nThrough cedar groves where spirits softly go\nAt Okunoin’s hall where lanterns softly gleam\nThou’lt walk with ancestors through mist and dream\n\n---\n**Day the Fifth: To Nature’s Lap Where Earth and Sky Embrace**\nWhere cherry blossoms drift on winds so light\nIn Hiroshima’s Miyajima ‘neath petals white\nOr autumn’s hues in Kyoto’s hills arrayed\nWith maples blaze where poets often strayed\n\nTo Takayama’s streets where Edo’s past yet stays\nWith morning markets where the olden days\nStill whisper through the hands of craftsmen true\nAnd sake that flows as smooth as rivers new\n\n---\n**Day the Sixth: The Final Bow Before Thy Parting**\nTo Tokyo once more where skies of blue prevail\nOne last sushi feast to seal thy tale\nAt Odaiba’s edge where futurists have played\nWith giant screens and thrills that never fade\n\nAnd as thy ship doth cast thee back to shore\nRemember Japan’s grace forevermore\nWith temples old and cities bright and keen\nA land of dreams where earth meets heaven\n\n---\nFare thee well fair wanderer with thy heart so true\nMay Japan’s magic linger through thy days anew", "logprobs": [{"token": "H", "logprob": -0.16029712557792664}, {"token": "ark", "logprob": -0.0027155925054103136}, {"token": " ye", "logprob": -3.409248113632202}, {"token": " travel", "logprob": -0.5790791511535645}, {"token": "er", "logprob": -0.0005744237569160759}, {"token": " bold", "logprob": -0.4664765000343323}, {"token": " whose", "logprob": -2.412137985229492}, {"token": " heart", "logprob": -0.312180489301681